    <string name="main_title">Voice Control</string>
    <string name="main_subtitle">Talk to your phone. It does the tapping.</string>
    <string name="how_to_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="how_to_body">Grant the permissions below, then tap Start overlay. A blue mic bubble floats over every app. Tap it and say what you want done, for example \"turn on Wi-Fi\" or \"search Chrome for the weather in Berlin\". The assistant may ask a quick question, then it operates the phone for you. While it works, the bubble shrinks to a thin bar at the top of the screen; tap ■ there to stop it. Drag the bubble anywhere and it snaps to the nearest edge. Tap it again to end the conversation.</string>
